@frmu1970 It's simple: if you have version 2.78 of Blender, then you download the BFB Addon (alternative model file for zt2), remembering that it has to be this version because it doesn't work on the others, and you also have to have zt2 for it to work.

Then you save it as an fbx file.

And that's it, you have a zt2 animal to put in games or animations.

